<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        Printed-check positioning and content tweaks requested by UFS.

        Injected as a stylesheet into the check face template
        (l10n_us_check_printing.ckus_check). Positioning uses margin and
        absolute `top` only, never CSS `transform`: the check report is
        qweb-pdf (wkhtmltopdf), whose engine silently drops transforms, so
        transform-based nudges show in the browser preview but not on the
        printed check. margin and `top` are honored, and are how the base
        layout positions every field.

        Calibrated to UFS's pre-printed check stock:

        1. Whole printout down a quarter inch. The page article carries the
           company Check Margins as position: relative; top; we add a 0.25in
           top margin so the check face and both stubs drop together.

        2. Check face fields down an eighth inch more. The date, payee, amount
           and written amount are shifted by the check face container
           (.ckus_check, base top about 0) set to top: 0.105in. Its sibling
           stubs are not affected, so only the check face moves. The fields end
           up three eighths of an inch below the base layout (quarter from the
           page margin plus the eighth here).

        3. Payee address into the #9 window. Base top is 1.65in. The container
           shift in step 2 would carry the address down with the fields, so its
           own top is raised to 2.025in to cancel that and leave the net
           address three quarters of an inch below the base layout, clearing
           the window while the fields above it stay put.

        4. Invoices off the check face. When a check pays several bills their
           numbers render on the memo line (.ckus_memo); display:none, which
           wkhtmltopdf honors, hides them. The remittance stub keeps the list.

        Calibration knobs for a future test print: the 0.25in page margin
        (whole printout) and the two tops, .ckus_check 0.105in (the fields) and
        .ckus_payee_addr 2.025in (the address). Raise/lower .ckus_check to move
        the fields, and change .ckus_payee_addr by the same amount in the
        opposite direction to keep the address put. Covers the Print Check
        (Top) layout UFS uses.

        NOTE: this report has attachment_use=true, so a printed check's PDF is
        cached on the payment and reused on reprint. After changing this file,
        delete the cached PDFs of already-printed checks (Settings > Technical
        > Attachments, name contains _top.pdf) or they reprint with the old
        layout. New checks always render fresh.
    -->
    <template id="ckus_check_ufs_tweaks"
              inherit_id="l10n_us_check_printing.ckus_check">
        <xpath expr="//div[hasclass('ckus_check')]" position="inside">
            <style>
                .ckus_top_page { margin-top: 0.25in !important; }
                .ckus_check { top: 0.105in !important; transform: none !important; }
                .ckus_payee_addr { top: 2.025in !important; transform: none !important; }
                .ckus_memo { display: none !important; }
            </style>
        </xpath>
    </template>
</odoo>
